      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. marie antoinette feels a bit too... well, too public? i dont feel like a queen. more like someone in the shadows, someone who was actually pulling the strings or advising the people in charge. i remember feeling this incredible pressure to get the wording of a treaty exactly right so it wouldn't trigger a war. \n\nim not looking for the most famous names, more like the influential advisors or diplomats. someone who was very observant, maybe a bit cynical, and knew how to read a room perfectly. can you look for people like that? maybe someone who worked during the transition from the monarchy to the revolution?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
